{"module":"rights","voice":"male","duration":231.5,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Your rights with police, and after a weaponized call","start":0.0,"end":3.9,"words":[[0.05,0.23],[0.23,0.68],[0.68,0.96],[0.96,1.5],[1.82,2.09],[2.09,2.45],[2.45,2.63],[2.63,3.45],[3.45,3.72]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This is general information about U.S. law, not legal advice, and laws differ by state.","start":4.7,"end":11.56,"words":[[4.75,4.98],[4.98,5.13],[5.13,5.74],[5.74,6.5],[6.5,6.88],[6.88,7.26],[7.64,7.86],[8.13,8.36],[8.36,8.74],[8.74,9.27],[9.53,9.76],[9.76,9.99],[9.99,10.29],[10.29,10.52],[10.52,10.98]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The goal of every encounter is to get home safely; you can challenge what happened later.","start":11.91,"end":17.61,"words":[[11.96,12.11],[12.11,12.4],[12.4,12.55],[12.55,12.84],[12.84,13.42],[13.42,13.57],[13.57,13.71],[13.71,13.93],[13.93,14.22],[14.22,14.74],[14.99,15.14],[15.14,15.36],[15.36,15.94],[15.94,16.16],[16.16,16.6],[16.6,17.04]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Free, detailed guides from the ACLU and others are linked on the Take action page.","start":17.96,"end":23.47,"words":[[17.99,18.31],[18.59,19.14],[19.14,19.54],[19.54,19.86],[19.86,20.02],[20.02,20.33],[20.33,20.57],[20.57,20.89],[20.89,20.97],[20.97,21.37],[21.37,21.52],[21.52,21.68],[21.68,22.0],[22.0,22.4],[22.4,22.87]]},{"el":"h0","text":"If police stop you on the street","start":23.82,"end":25.93,"words":[[23.87,24.04],[24.04,24.46],[24.46,24.8],[24.8,24.97],[24.97,25.14],[25.14,25.31],[25.31,25.73]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Police may briefly stop you if they have “reasonable suspicion” that you're involved in a crime, and may pat down your outer clothing if they believe you're armed (Terry v. Ohio, 1968).","start":26.63,"end":39.42,"words":[[26.68,27.08],[27.08,27.31],[27.31,27.79],[27.79,28.11],[28.11,28.27],[28.27,28.43],[28.43,28.66],[28.66,28.9],[28.9,29.62],[29.62,30.25],[30.25,30.49],[30.49,30.65],[30.65,31.2],[31.2,31.36],[31.36,31.52],[31.52,32.0],[32.28,32.51],[32.51,32.75],[32.75,32.99],[32.99,33.31],[33.31,33.47],[33.47,33.78],[33.78,34.34],[34.34,34.5],[34.5,34.74],[34.74,35.13],[35.13,35.29],[35.29,35.53],[35.53,35.85],[35.85,36.09],[36.48,37.12],[37.39,38.82]]},{"el":"s0","text":"You can ask, “Am I free to go?”","start":39.77,"end":43.05,"words":[[39.82,40.02],[40.02,40.33],[40.33,40.73],[41.08,41.28],[41.28,41.48],[41.48,41.78],[41.78,41.98],[41.98,42.38]]},{"el":"s0","text":"If yes, you may calmly leave.","start":43.4,"end":46.36,"words":[[43.45,43.64],[43.64,44.01],[44.35,44.53],[44.53,44.82],[44.82,45.29],[45.29,45.67]]},{"el":"s0","text":"You have the right to remain silent, but the Supreme Court has said you must say you are using it (Salinas v. Texas, 2013): “I'm going to remain silent.”","start":46.71,"end":57.74,"words":[[46.76,46.91],[46.91,47.14],[47.14,47.29],[47.29,47.6],[47.6,47.75],[47.75,48.21],[48.21,48.83],[49.09,49.32],[49.32,49.48],[49.48,49.94],[49.94,50.17],[50.17,50.4],[50.4,50.63],[50.63,50.78],[50.78,51.09],[51.09,51.32],[51.32,51.47],[51.47,51.55],[51.55,51.93],[51.93,52.08],[52.08,52.7],[52.7,52.93],[53.31,53.85],[54.11,55.03],[55.3,55.53],[55.53,55.91],[55.91,56.07],[56.07,56.53],[56.53,57.14]]},{"el":"s0","text":"About half the states have “stop and identify” laws that require you to give your name when lawfully stopped (Hiibel, 2004).","start":58.09,"end":68.14,"words":[[58.13,58.6],[58.6,58.88],[58.88,59.07],[59.07,59.64],[59.64,59.92],[59.92,60.3],[60.3,60.59],[60.59,61.53],[61.53,61.82],[61.82,62.1],[62.1,62.76],[62.76,62.95],[62.95,63.14],[63.14,63.43],[63.43,63.62],[63.62,63.99],[63.99,64.28],[64.28,64.85],[64.85,65.32],[65.32,66.08],[66.41,67.54]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Searches, cars and your home","start":69.04,"end":71.71,"words":[[69.09,69.85],[70.22,70.55],[70.55,70.87],[70.87,71.08],[71.08,71.52]]},{"el":"s1","text":"You can say, “I don't consent to a search.”","start":72.41,"end":76.71,"words":[[72.45,72.65],[72.65,72.96],[72.96,73.37],[73.72,73.92],[73.92,74.43],[74.43,75.14],[75.14,75.34],[75.34,75.55],[75.55,76.05]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Saying it doesn't stop an officer who has other legal grounds, but it preserves your rights for court.","start":77.06,"end":83.05,"words":[[77.08,77.45],[77.45,77.6],[77.6,78.04],[78.04,78.34],[78.34,78.49],[78.49,78.86],[78.86,79.01],[79.01,79.23],[79.23,79.45],[79.45,79.82],[79.82,80.42],[80.68,80.9],[80.9,81.05],[81.05,81.57],[81.57,81.72],[81.72,82.09],[82.09,82.24],[82.24,82.53]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In a traffic stop, the driver must show a license, registration and proof of insurance when asked.","start":83.4,"end":90.97,"words":[[83.45,83.61],[83.61,83.77],[83.77,84.27],[84.27,84.67],[84.96,85.12],[85.12,85.61],[85.61,85.94],[85.94,86.18],[86.18,86.35],[86.35,87.0],[87.29,88.35],[88.35,88.59],[88.59,88.92],[88.92,89.08],[89.08,89.82],[89.82,90.06],[90.06,90.47]]},{"el":"s1","text":"At home, you don't have to open the door unless officers have a warrant signed by a judge; ask them to slide it under the door or hold it to a window.","start":91.32,"end":101.58,"words":[[91.37,91.54],[91.54,91.95],[92.25,92.41],[92.41,92.83],[92.83,93.08],[93.08,93.25],[93.25,93.67],[93.67,93.84],[93.84,94.01],[94.01,94.42],[94.42,94.93],[94.93,95.18],[95.18,95.34],[95.34,95.85],[95.85,96.27],[96.27,96.52],[96.52,96.68],[96.68,97.19],[97.48,97.73],[97.73,97.98],[97.98,98.15],[98.15,98.57],[98.57,98.74],[98.74,99.07],[99.07,99.24],[99.24,99.41],[99.41,99.49],[99.49,99.91],[99.91,100.08],[100.08,100.24],[100.24,100.41],[100.41,101.0]]},{"el":"s1","text":"An immigration (ICE) administrative warrant signed by an officer, not a judge, does not by itself allow entry into a home.","start":101.93,"end":111.59,"words":[[101.98,102.15],[102.15,103.0],[103.0,103.25],[103.55,104.66],[104.66,105.17],[105.17,105.59],[105.59,105.84],[105.84,106.01],[106.01,106.52],[106.82,107.08],[107.08,107.25],[107.25,107.76],[108.05,108.31],[108.31,108.56],[108.56,108.82],[108.82,109.33],[109.33,109.67],[109.67,110.09],[110.09,110.43],[110.43,110.6],[110.6,111.02]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Recording the police","start":112.49,"end":113.95,"words":[[112.54,113.14],[113.14,113.32],[113.32,113.75]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Several federal appeals courts have recognized a First Amendment right to record police doing their jobs in public, starting with Glik v. Cunniffe (2011).","start":114.65,"end":125.61,"words":[[114.7,115.18],[115.18,115.73],[115.73,116.12],[116.12,116.44],[116.44,116.68],[116.68,117.47],[117.47,117.62],[117.62,117.94],[117.94,118.65],[118.65,118.97],[118.97,119.12],[119.12,119.52],[119.52,119.91],[119.91,120.23],[120.23,120.47],[120.47,120.86],[120.86,121.02],[121.02,121.57],[121.85,122.32],[122.32,122.56],[122.56,122.87],[122.87,123.11],[123.5,123.9],[123.9,125.0]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Keep a safe distance, don't interfere, and say out loud that you're recording if asked.","start":125.96,"end":132.04,"words":[[125.98,126.22],[126.22,126.38],[126.38,126.7],[126.7,127.34],[127.63,128.03],[128.03,128.67],[128.95,129.19],[129.19,129.43],[129.43,129.67],[129.67,129.99],[129.99,130.23],[130.23,130.39],[130.39,130.95],[130.95,131.11],[131.11,131.51]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Many weaponized 911 calls became public only because someone recorded them.","start":132.39,"end":138.42,"words":[[132.44,132.72],[132.72,133.38],[133.38,134.75],[134.75,135.04],[135.04,135.47],[135.47,135.91],[135.91,136.27],[136.27,136.63],[136.63,137.06],[137.06,137.57],[137.57,137.86]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Staying as safe as possible","start":139.32,"end":141.54,"words":[[139.37,139.94],[139.94,140.13],[140.13,140.51],[140.51,140.7],[140.7,141.36]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Keep your hands visible, and don't run, argue or physically resist, even if you believe the stop is wrong.","start":142.24,"end":149.24,"words":[[142.26,142.49],[142.49,142.64],[142.64,143.03],[143.03,143.64],[143.91,144.14],[144.14,144.53],[144.53,144.83],[145.1,145.41],[145.41,145.49],[145.49,146.02],[146.02,146.56],[146.83,147.14],[147.14,147.29],[147.29,147.44],[147.44,147.83],[147.83,147.98],[147.98,148.29],[148.29,148.44],[148.44,148.75]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Tell officers before you reach for anything: “My license is in my back pocket.”","start":149.59,"end":154.08,"words":[[149.63,149.84],[149.84,150.25],[150.25,150.52],[150.52,150.66],[150.66,150.93],[150.93,151.07],[151.07,151.55],[151.79,151.99],[151.99,152.47],[152.47,152.61],[152.61,152.75],[152.75,152.95],[152.95,153.16],[153.16,153.57]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Don't lie or give false documents.","start":154.43,"end":157.34,"words":[[154.48,154.9],[154.9,155.14],[155.14,155.23],[155.23,155.48],[155.48,155.81],[155.81,156.71]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Teach children what to do, and agree on a family plan for who to call.","start":157.69,"end":162.48,"words":[[157.73,158.04],[158.04,158.65],[158.65,158.89],[158.89,159.04],[159.04,159.27],[159.54,159.77],[159.77,160.08],[160.08,160.24],[160.24,160.39],[160.39,160.86],[160.86,161.17],[161.17,161.32],[161.32,161.48],[161.48,161.63],[161.63,161.94]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Remember officer names, badge and car numbers, and witnesses' names.","start":162.83,"end":168.4,"words":[[162.89,163.48],[163.48,163.91],[163.91,164.41],[164.71,165.05],[165.05,165.3],[165.3,165.47],[165.47,166.06],[166.36,166.61],[166.61,167.29],[167.29,167.8]]},{"el":"h4","text":"If someone called the police on you because of who you are","start":169.3,"end":172.89,"words":[[169.35,169.54],[169.54,170.12],[170.12,170.5],[170.5,170.69],[170.69,171.16],[171.16,171.35],[171.35,171.54],[171.54,172.02],[172.02,172.21],[172.21,172.4],[172.4,172.59],[172.59,172.69]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Write it all down as soon as you can: date, time, place, what the caller said, what officers did, names and badge numbers, and witnesses.","start":173.59,"end":182.84,"words":[[173.64,173.92],[173.92,174.07],[174.07,174.21],[174.21,174.49],[174.49,174.63],[174.63,174.84],[174.84,174.99],[174.99,175.13],[175.13,175.41],[175.66,176.01],[176.26,176.61],[176.86,177.28],[177.53,177.74],[177.74,177.89],[177.89,178.17],[178.17,178.45],[178.7,178.91],[178.91,179.34],[179.34,179.62],[179.87,180.22],[180.22,180.43],[180.43,180.72],[180.72,181.21],[181.46,181.67],[181.67,182.31]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Save evidence: your video and anyone else's, photos, and texts.","start":183.19,"end":188.71,"words":[[183.24,183.55],[183.55,184.17],[184.44,184.59],[184.59,185.13],[185.13,185.36],[185.36,185.82],[185.82,186.28],[186.55,187.16],[187.43,187.66],[187.66,188.2]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Request the records: the 911 recording and the call log are usually public records; use the request template in the toolkit.","start":189.06,"end":197.33,"words":[[189.11,189.58],[189.58,189.72],[189.72,190.19],[190.42,190.56],[190.56,191.84],[191.84,192.31],[192.31,192.51],[192.51,192.64],[192.64,192.85],[192.85,193.05],[193.05,193.12],[193.12,193.59],[193.59,193.99],[193.99,194.46],[194.7,194.9],[194.9,195.03],[195.03,195.51],[195.51,196.04],[196.04,196.18],[196.18,196.31],[196.31,196.78]]},{"el":"s4","text":"File a complaint about officer conduct with the department's internal affairs office or your city's civilian oversight board.","start":197.68,"end":205.84,"words":[[197.7,198.03],[198.03,198.19],[198.19,198.93],[198.93,199.34],[199.34,199.76],[199.76,200.33],[200.33,200.58],[200.58,200.75],[200.75,201.57],[201.57,202.15],[202.15,202.56],[202.56,202.89],[202.89,202.97],[202.97,203.14],[203.14,203.55],[203.55,204.21],[204.21,204.87],[204.87,205.2]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Get legal advice: in San Francisco, Oregon and New York, laws let you bring a civil claim against the caller; elsewhere other claims may apply.","start":206.19,"end":216.72,"words":[[206.24,206.48],[206.48,206.88],[206.88,207.45],[207.73,207.9],[207.9,208.14],[208.14,209.03],[209.31,209.8],[209.8,210.04],[210.04,210.28],[210.28,210.61],[210.89,211.13],[211.13,211.38],[211.38,211.54],[211.54,211.86],[211.86,212.02],[212.02,212.43],[212.43,212.83],[212.83,213.32],[213.32,213.48],[213.48,213.88],[214.17,214.65],[214.65,214.9],[214.9,215.38],[215.38,215.62],[215.62,216.11]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Legal aid, the ACLU or the NAACP can help you find a lawyer.","start":217.07,"end":221.8,"words":[[217.12,217.49],[217.49,217.79],[218.06,218.21],[218.21,218.51],[218.51,218.58],[218.58,218.73],[218.73,219.71],[219.71,219.93],[219.93,220.23],[220.23,220.38],[220.38,220.76],[220.76,220.91],[220.91,221.28]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Tell your story, if you want to, on the Stories page and to your lawmakers.","start":222.15,"end":228.39,"words":[[222.21,222.49],[222.49,222.67],[222.67,223.23],[223.55,223.73],[223.73,223.92],[223.92,224.28],[224.28,224.56],[224.88,225.06],[225.06,225.25],[225.25,225.8],[225.8,226.26],[226.26,226.54],[226.54,226.72],[226.72,226.9],[226.9,227.73]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Stories pass laws.","start":228.74,"end":230.57,"words":[[228.78,229.32],[229.32,229.59],[229.59,229.95]]}]}